    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d7">

                <pb facs="0047" n="10" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v05/pg10"/>

                <head>7. Memorandum From the President’s Counsel (Ehrlichman) to Secretary of State
                        Rogers<anchor n="1" xml:id="d7-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1969-09-30">September 30, 1969</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The President has weighed the international and domestic political considerations
                    relating to the proposed expansion of the U.N. Building.</p>
                <p>In view of the construction moratorium and the war on inflation, he has decided
                    not to approve the funding for this project at this time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">John D. Ehrlichman</hi>
                        <anchor n="2" xml:id="d7-f2"/>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
